1. GRANT
Subject to payment and to this licence, the publisher grants the purchaser a
perpetual, non exclusive, non transferable licence to install and use the product
for the internal business operations of one business owned or operated by the
purchaser, on any number of devices the purchaser personally controls.

2. PERMITTED USE
The purchaser may modify the product, create derivative tools, workspaces and
commands for their own use, and retain those modifications. The purchaser may
retain and use any version received, indefinitely, whether or not the publisher
continues to distribute or support the product.

2A. EXTENSIONS BY THE PURCHASER
Plugins, adapters, workspaces, tools, commands and migrations authored by the
purchaser are the exclusive property of the purchaser, whether or not they depend
on the product's interfaces, and may be distributed or sold by the purchaser
without further permission. This clause does not permit distribution of any part
of the product itself.

2B. THIRD PARTY EXTENSIONS
Extensions authored by parties other than the publisher are not part of the
product, are not warranted by the publisher, and are used at the purchaser's own
risk. The publisher makes no representation about their behaviour, security or
fitness. The verification facilities in the product check declared metadata and
checksums only, and do not constitute an assurance of safety.

3. RESTRICTIONS
The purchaser may not: distribute, sell, sublicense, lease, or publish the
product or any derivative of it; offer the product or a derivative as a hosted or
managed service to third parties; operate the product on behalf of another
business for a fee without a separate written agreement; or remove licence or
attribution files from any copy.

4. PURCHASER DATA
All content created by the purchaser under the data directory is the exclusive
property of the purchaser. The product operates entirely on the purchaser's own
devices. The publisher does not receive, store, transmit or process purchaser
data, and has no access to it. No account is created and no telemetry is
collected.

5. UPDATES
The publisher will make updates to the current major version available to the
purchaser for a minimum of twelve months from the date of purchase. The publisher
is not obliged to publish updates beyond that period. No update requires the
purchaser to replace or surrender their data.

6. SUPPORT
Support is provided by email with a target response time of two working days, and
covers installation, defects, and the intended operation of the product. It does
not include accounting, tax, legal, pricing or business advice.

7. REFUND
The purchaser may request a full refund within thirty days of purchase for any
reason. No return or deletion of files is required as a condition of refund.

8. NO PROFESSIONAL ADVICE
The product performs arithmetic over data supplied by the purchaser and presents
the result. It does not provide accounting, tax, legal, financial or regulatory
advice. Figures described as tax set aside are a planning percentage chosen by
the purchaser applied to cash receipts recorded by the purchaser, and are not a
computation of any liability. The purchaser is responsible for verifying all
figures and for their own compliance obligations.

9. WARRANTY
The product is provided as is. To the maximum extent permitted by law the
publisher disclaims all implied warranties, including merchantability, fitness
for a particular purpose, and non infringement. Nothing in this licence excludes
liability which cannot lawfully be excluded, including for fraud or for death or
personal injury caused by negligence.

10. LIABILITY
To the maximum extent permitted by law, the publisher's total aggregate liability
arising out of or in connection with this licence is limited to the amount paid
by the purchaser for the product. The publisher is not liable for loss of profit,
loss of business, loss of data, or indirect or consequential loss.

11. TERMINATION
This licence terminates automatically if the purchaser breaches section 3. On
termination the purchaser must cease use and destroy all copies of the product.
Purchaser data is unaffected and remains the property of the purchaser.

12. ASSIGNMENT AND SURVIVAL
The publisher may assign this licence in connection with a sale or transfer of
the product. The purchaser's rights under sections 1, 2 and 4 survive any such
transfer and any discontinuation of the product.

13. ENTIRE AGREEMENT
This licence, together with the plain writing summary distributed as
LICENCE-PLAIN.md, is the entire agreement between the parties. Where the two
differ, the plain writing summary reflects the intended meaning.
